question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128383"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330500/selection/0b8aa62f5ec2a70f4c33ed079a6e99d28bbb65c39c1e6957969ab02fbcf1acc8" :answer/id #uuid "4b2bacdd-6cb8-50d4-8afa-5d4d7bc3e608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+y-10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330500/selection/26e8b6600d7170808fa84aff09382d96bcd607b518e08d8288f11c60859e5970" :answer/id #uuid "65efd500-d89f-5b07-ae17-7ca8d5c2fe7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-6y-10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330500/selection/e5f6f8c6073bcae61ae5fa1103baef849d10899d869d06cd00ea4552b2ccd5fe" :answer/id #uuid "b30c4d34-7509-5372-aa3a-3f0d318eaf69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-2y+z-10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330500/selection/add53719cca255e979bec1817676334e61f9068a61c3ed788cad0074fa661b94" :answer/id #uuid "ff97a1c2-3ba8-50b5-9630-7c229350dc78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-2y-10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330500/selection/f88d2146687f5056f5820ac55f1278b2b81e32dd8ee3d5b305f2e8b0754a5b8c" :answer/id #uuid "12a26a86-a380-5d97-8b3e-f14defa24e02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x-y-10z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330500/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f8355a-f47d-5fde-944c-7f01b71f1f6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-330500/selection/add53719cca255e979bec1817676334e61f9068a61c3ed788cad0074fa661b94" :answer-field/choices ["q-330500/selection/0b8aa62f5ec2a70f4c33ed079a6e99d28bbb65c39c1e6957969ab02fbcf1acc8" "q-330500/selection/26e8b6600d7170808fa84aff09382d96bcd607b518e08d8288f11c60859e5970" "q-330500/selection/e5f6f8c6073bcae61ae5fa1103baef849d10899d869d06cd00ea4552b2ccd5fe" "q-330500/selection/add53719cca255e979bec1817676334e61f9068a61c3ed788cad0074fa661b94" "q-330500/selection/f88d2146687f5056f5820ac55f1278b2b81e32dd8ee3d5b305f2e8b0754a5b8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330500" :question/id #uuid "e5f496f5-82da-5347-a9dc-1d7749662c5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-330500" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,1,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨2,1,-5⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =⟨2,1,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =10 \\\\ 6x-2y & =10 \\\\ 6x-2y-10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330500/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330500"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336358/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "f7d4c5e8-f936-53a9-bc5f-3cca97c3b2c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336358/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "18d0d219-ec4f-53bb-97f0-b1c5bd529520" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336358/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-336358/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336358/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "3f369a1e-a1c1-580a-b60d-5664c6315eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336358/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "842469ef-6b3f-52d4-b990-df6cd1e2c154" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336358/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-336358/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336358/field-3/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "c637def1-cd89-5a2f-83b5-1ab8c3027aad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336358/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c362e1f6-816b-5c65-bc37-a382d6255263" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336358/field-3/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer-field/choices ["q-336358/field-3/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336358" :question/id #uuid "bc0bcd5d-4d1d-5e96-9f96-539ff833a355" :question/math-academy-id "q-336358" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-4,3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-3,-6⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,-8⟩.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$y\\,+\\,z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-4,3,5⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =36i+16j+4k \\\\  & =⟨36,16,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =⟨-4,3,5⟩\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =-76\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =-76 \\\\ 36x+16y+4z & =-76 \\\\ 36x+16y+4z+76 & =0 \\\\ 9x+4y+z+19 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336358/field-1" "q-336358/field-2" "q-336358/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0efe5b11-2c87-58e9-bf7c-e1eecb07adf2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336358"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336407/selection/98a847554fa470e1e5b1a99c06cf8370fd7a9c9957e26945e92d9c476003bc40" :answer/id #uuid "5a938bfe-8aab-5fb8-b67e-43d647955b92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+y+2z-3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336407/selection/4b2de299d3a65887625bc978c4d72b792d4dd28a061212d58b550610cd96ee74" :answer/id #uuid "7ba28ff5-ac52-516d-924d-c3aac3509bb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+y-2z-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336407/selection/f20673cb0c4108af93eefb2a34bca621a405bf233772bfbac7eab44408254183" :answer/id #uuid "7536e066-849c-5735-87e5-0b7eb1d522d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-y-2z-3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336407/selection/68a8addc4fab3c99fb49f658d40cb28bf1a8e5c45868c99f5ff4f9cbe78eee9d" :answer/id #uuid "4d7bf099-5abd-5ebb-b7b8-f635a931e376" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+y-2z-3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336407/selection/e77137244dca22b6feee63c47d21aea88e34eb3bc8cc3d5853e4178d4a60b2e4" :answer/id #uuid "615827cd-5437-576d-ac3c-41111e651999" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-2z-6=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336407/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4538f7fa-876c-5ec8-825c-2a661cb26038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-336407/selection/e77137244dca22b6feee63c47d21aea88e34eb3bc8cc3d5853e4178d4a60b2e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-336407/selection/98a847554fa470e1e5b1a99c06cf8370fd7a9c9957e26945e92d9c476003bc40" "q-336407/selection/4b2de299d3a65887625bc978c4d72b792d4dd28a061212d58b550610cd96ee74" "q-336407/selection/f20673cb0c4108af93eefb2a34bca621a405bf233772bfbac7eab44408254183" "q-336407/selection/68a8addc4fab3c99fb49f658d40cb28bf1a8e5c45868c99f5ff4f9cbe78eee9d" "q-336407/selection/e77137244dca22b6feee63c47d21aea88e34eb3bc8cc3d5853e4178d4a60b2e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336407" :question/id #uuid "d501cbc7-e6c3-5ee6-bf3b-290a3eeec39d" :question/math-academy-id "q-336407" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,1⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨4,0,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is\n\n$$\nn=⟨4,0,-2⟩,\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =⟨2,-3,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute  $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =3 \\\\ 4x-2z & =6 \\\\ 4x-2z-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336407/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
